<http://data.silknow.org/object/5760cd2f-94ac-3868-88f4-7d24b4a925bf/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Dress of buff silk with a self-coloured pattern bound in a twill and with a bold meander of brocade floral stems filling the width of the silk. Length of repeat 36<sup>1/2\".\n</sup>The dress has been completely remade into a conventional 1840 dress with a low, round neck, short tight sleeves, pointed bodice and organ pleated skirt. The bodice is linen lined, boned and has eyelets for a lace fastening at the back."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/5760cd2f-94ac-3868-88f4-7d24b4a925bf> .

